      "levelTitle": "JHS 2: Factorization & Fractional Equations",
      "summary": "Common factor extraction, four-term grouping factorization, difference of two squares, and fractional linear equations.",
      "notes": "### 1. Factorization by Highest Common Factor (HCF)\nTo factorize an expression, identify the highest common factor of numbers and variables:\n$$6x^2y - 9xy^2 = 3xy(2x - 3y)$$\n\n### 2. Four-Term Factorization by Grouping\nGroup the four terms into pairs that share a common binomial factor:\n$$ax + ay + bx + by = a(x + y) + b(x + y) = (x + y)(a + b)$$\n\n### 3. Difference of Two Squares\n$$a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)$$\n\n### 4. Fractional Linear Equations\nMultiply through by the **Lowest Common Multiple (LCM)** of all denominators to eliminate fractions before solving.",
      "workedExamples": [
        {
          "id": "we_alg_j2_01",
          "title": "Four-Term Factorization by Grouping",
          "problem": "Factorize completely: $4a^2 + 3ab - 8ac - 6bc$.",
          "steps": [
            "Group terms pairwise: $(4a^2 + 3ab) - (8ac + 6bc)$.",
            "Factor out the common term from the first pair: $a(4a + 3b)$.",
            "Factor out $-2c$ from the second pair: $-2c(4a + 3b)$.",
            "Notice the identical binomial factor $(4a + 3b)$ and combine: $(4a + 3b)(a - 2c)$."
          ],
          "finalAnswer": "$$(4a + 3b)(a - 2c)$$"
        },
        {
          "id": "we_alg_j2_02",
          "title": "Solving Fractional Linear Equations",
          "problem": "Solve for $x$ in: $\\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{2x}{5} - \\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "steps": [
            "Identify the denominators: 3, 5, and 2. Their LCM is 30.",
            "Multiply every term by 30: $30\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right) + 30\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right) = 30\\left(\\frac{2x}{5}\\right) - 30\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$.",
            "Simplify each term: $10x + 12 = 12x - 15$.",
            "Rearrange terms: $12 + 15 = 12x - 10x$.",
            "Solve for $x$: $27 = 2x \\implies x = \\frac{27}{2} = 13.5$."
          ],
          "finalAnswer": "$$x = \\frac{27}{2} = 13.5$$"
        }
      ],
