      "notes": "### 1. Quadratic Factorization ($ax^2 + bx + c$)\n1. Find two numbers that multiply to give $ac$ and add to give $b$.\n2. Split the middle term $bx$ into two terms.\n3. Factorize by grouping in pairs.\n\n### 2. Simultaneous Linear Equations\nTwo methods:\n- **Elimination Method:** Multiply equations so coefficients of one variable match, then add or subtract.\n- **Substitution Method:** Express one variable in terms of the other from one equation and substitute into the second.\n\n### 3. Change of Subject of a Formula\nIsolate the required variable on one side of the equation:\n- Clear fractions by multiplying by the LCM.\n- Clear brackets.\n- Collect all terms containing the target variable on one side.\n- Factorize out the target variable.\n- Divide by the coefficient/binomial multiplier.",
